# Citation metadata for Isocenter.
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file.
# Schema reference: https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# Isocenter is the upstream half of a pair: it builds and de-identifies
# the corpus that Murmur Studio (10.5281/zenodo.21077528) reviews. Work
# that used both should cite both -- the de-identification tooling is a
# methods citation, not a courtesy.
#
# `doi:` carries the CONCEPT DOI -- the parent record that always
# resolves to the latest version -- not the per-version DOI minted
# alongside each release. A citation should follow the work, not freeze
# on whichever version happened to be current when it was written;
# readers who need the exact version can reach it from the concept
# record. Per-version DOIs live alongside their release on Zenodo.
#
# Do not change this to a version DOI, and do not guess one: a DOI here
# that does not resolve is worse than none, because this file is what
# tooling copies into bibliographies.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Isocenter in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Isocenter"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for indexing, de-identifying, and exporting DICOM
  datasets at cohort scale. Builds a SQLite metadata index and a binary
  pixel/waveform sidecar over a read-only source tree, applies DICOM
  PS3.15 de-identification profiles and machine-specific pixel redaction
  in memory, and writes clean copies to a new directory. Exports DICOM or
  PhysioNet WFDB, including a waveform annotation bridge to Murmur
  Studio. Source data is never modified.
type: software
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/kvnlng/Isocenter"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22104298"
url: "https://kvnlng.github.io/Isocenter/"
keywords:
  - DICOM
  - de-identification
  - anonymization
  - PHI
  - HIPAA
  - WFDB
  - ECG
  - medical-imaging
  - research-software
authors:
  - family-names: Long
    given-names: Kevin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8881-2481"
version: 0.9.2
date-released: 2026-09-05
